title: Zinoviev against Radek
subtitle: A quarrel on the Executive reaches the German districts.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 11 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and ending_id = 0 and comintern_member = 1 and e20_quarrel_line = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_quarrel_zin_ahead = Q.ecci_zinoviev > Q.ecci_radek ? 1 : 0;
!}

= Zinoviev against Radek

Zinoviev came home from Halle a hero. In *Pravda* he writes that the German party must go on the offensive with the Independents' masses behind it. Radek answers that a mass party needs a year to learn to walk, and that whoever sends it into battle before then will lose it.

Letters from both men are passed round the German districts. The Left quotes Zinoviev at every meeting, and the Right quotes Radek. [? if e20_quarrel_zin_ahead = 1 : On the Executive, Zinoviev's friends are winning. ?][? if e20_quarrel_zin_ahead = 0 : On the Executive, Radek has Lenin's ear. ?]

- @radek: Side with Radek.
- @zinoviev: Side with Zinoviev.
- @publish: Print both letters, and say the German party decides for itself.

@radek
subtitle: Our Left will say we chose the cautious man.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_quarrel_line = 1;
RG.ecci('radek', 10);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -10);
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Radek is grateful. Zinoviev has the Zentrale's letter copied for his files.

@zinoviev
subtitle: He is President of the International, and he remembers his friends.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_quarrel_line = 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 12);
RG.ecci('radek', -8);
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Zinoviev's article goes on our front page with a note from the Zentrale agreeing with it. Levi's friends begin to worry about the spring.

@publish
subtitle: The whole Executive will be irritated.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_quarrel_line = 3;
RG.ecci('all', -5);
Q.independence += 6;
!}

Both letters appear side by side, with a short editorial. In Moscow the two men agree on one thing, which is that the German Zentrale has overstepped.
